From: phoenix port <fix@me>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: clear USB51 mode for non-SDP chargers

USBIN_ICL_OPTIONS.USB51_MODE caps the input current at 500mA
(USB 2.0 mode). The init sequence leaves it cleared, but the bit is
observed to become set again once a charger attaches.

smb_status_change_work() programs a proper ICL for the detected
charger type (battery-info value for DCP) but never touches this
option, so the hardware silently clamps the input back to 500mA.
With a ~450mA system load there is no net charge current and the
charger latches INHIBIT_CHARGE: STATUS stays 'Full' while the
battery drains, on every wall charger (reproducible across replug,
driver reload and reboot on PM6150/phoenix).

Clear USB51_MODE whenever the detected type is not SDP. Applied on
top of the recharge-bounce fix; both touch status_change_work.

Signed-off-by: phoenix port <fix@me>
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -560,6 +560,19 @@ static void smb_status_change_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * USBIN_ICL_OPTIONS.USB51_MODE caps the input current at 500mA
+	 * (USB 2.0 mode). It is valid for SDP only; leave it set for
+	 * CDP/DCP and the programmed ICL below gets silently clamped to
+	 * 500mA, leaving zero net charge current -- observed on PM6150
+	 * (phoenix): DCP chargers latched INHIBIT_CHARGE / STATUS=Full
+	 * forever while the battery drained.
+	 */
+	regmap_update_bits(chip->regmap, chip->base + USBIN_ICL_OPTIONS,
+			   USB51_MODE_BIT,
+			   charger_type == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_SDP ?
+			   USB51_MODE_BIT : 0);
+
 	smb_set_current_limit(chip, current_ua);
 
 	/*
